[{:db/id "q-134156/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "41a3d2e2-f9b1-5b0f-a8af-59094f708166" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134156/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "6912ce27-4c2c-5659-8670-f0090b9c8481" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134156/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "dfde804a-a975-53cd-a2c3-51f3c256f823" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134156/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "dc4eb2a6-0cf2-5ace-937d-557ac82e8807" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134156/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "474b4769-44a8-5d13-8bcc-2189d784e468" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134156/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3f3c1864-e7d4-5c97-bc7b-6f2ba2494195" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-134156/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-134156/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-134156/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-134156/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-134156/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-134156/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-134156" :question/id #uuid "73ee2d87-104f-5b41-bbb8-604f1e3cba8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-134156" :question/problem "Consider the following data sets:\n\n$$\nx={6,\\,4,\\,6,\\,8},\\,y={3,\\,4,\\,5,\\,8}\n$$\n\nYou're given that $\\overset{―}{x}=6$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=5.$ Calculate $\\text{Cov}(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(6-6)(3-5)+(4-6)(4-5)+(6-6)(5-5)+(8-6)(8-5)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(0)(-2)+(-2)(-1)+(0)(0)+(2)(3)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[0+2+0+6] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-134156/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2ac0065-9315-547a-a9cf-c6a5abea1aed"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-134156"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-134165/selection/f7ec98ce0d2d5e0413aaea93f098b04337f2217a14eff2f5b611bfb2fc659059" :answer/id #uuid "10cb9f08-9c8f-5d86-8420-98e257eaed50" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134165/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "8455dbb6-2eda-5055-929b-0bb78308c608" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134165/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "38ea8140-c0fb-56bc-a18c-80ee154525ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134165/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "2eaf9693-2f72-5292-aada-cc1788c3d28b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134165/selection/1b562e91f68bc228d59da280605802cc1ce0248d770285443e7d649fb5c75d13" :answer/id #uuid "a4cc824f-4c5a-58f2-8722-487fd8b0a394" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134165/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "79e46315-c012-5187-bb42-4e4e41818517" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-134165/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer-field/choices ["q-134165/selection/f7ec98ce0d2d5e0413aaea93f098b04337f2217a14eff2f5b611bfb2fc659059" "q-134165/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-134165/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-134165/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" "q-134165/selection/1b562e91f68bc228d59da280605802cc1ce0248d770285443e7d649fb5c75d13"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-134165" :question/id #uuid "8c9a493b-3f80-5d85-8627-a0cfaf455ca6" :question/math-academy-id "q-134165" :question/problem "Consider the following data sets:\n\n$$\nx={1,\\,4,\\,7,\\,12},\\,y={2,\\,4,\\,2,\\,8}\n$$\n\nYou're given that $\\overset{―}{x}=6$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=4.$ Calculate $\\text{Cov}(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(1-6)(2-4)+(4-6)(4-4)+(7-6)(2-4)+(12-6)(8-4)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-5)(-2)+(-2)(0)+(1)(-2)+(6)(4)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[10+0-2+24] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 32 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-134165/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2ac0065-9315-547a-a9cf-c6a5abea1aed"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-134165"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-134168/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer/id #uuid "cff689ec-4973-5191-b599-d6fa9b5f3593" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134168/selection/59cabed12271767d3647412725d382bc72464274dc4ac46b4e7903c969156a02" :answer/id #uuid "30c09cda-58cd-506d-bf61-6768b2fee2f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "19" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134168/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "725431a9-e973-5172-a01e-72e17b2a61e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134168/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "4a059e6e-e0a2-51e0-8c7a-7f5e012a0b4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134168/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "7859dddb-5f35-54e6-838d-fd8f46505934" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134168/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2886bb9c-3683-575b-a4a5-510e7a201322" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-134168/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer-field/choices ["q-134168/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" "q-134168/selection/59cabed12271767d3647412725d382bc72464274dc4ac46b4e7903c969156a02" "q-134168/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" "q-134168/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-134168/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-134168" :question/id #uuid "7661bdb4-4f12-5271-b8d5-fdde69eee899" :question/math-academy-id "q-134168" :question/problem "Calculate $\\text{Cov}(x,y)$ for the following data sets:\n\n$$\nx={-4,\\,2,\\,6,\\,8},\\,y={2,\\,-9,\\,3,\\,12}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the means:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot ((-4)+2+6+8) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =3 \\\\ \\overset{―}{y} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (2+(-9)+3+12) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-4-3)(2-2)+(2-3)(-9-2)+(6-3)(3-2)+(8-3)(12-2)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-7)(0)+(-1)(-11)+(3)(1)+(5)(10)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[0+11+3+50] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 64 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-134168/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2ac0065-9315-547a-a9cf-c6a5abea1aed"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-134168"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-134173/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "d534c4fa-3764-537c-9b1c-fde6b7be7f41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134173/selection/cca93330bdc2ff0543861ebace1767f4dbf656d494475323c839b42f25a3876a" :answer/id #uuid "5153f7f5-f08e-5660-be36-e10c86fc8ff6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134173/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "eeeb51d7-57c5-5560-b35e-5bf0fb2a4e34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134173/selection/ab3343a580c9ecbbb4e27d0c43b67b7d3815a6806a811b62927c9243c7c87034" :answer/id #uuid "bb3d0eb4-9621-5733-9e0b-1b60594abf48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134173/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "96f0ac24-be31-5e28-bdb0-42230ce81ebc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134173/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "27c678e2-9151-5984-bb0a-e3a87fb06293" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-134173/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer-field/choices ["q-134173/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-134173/selection/cca93330bdc2ff0543861ebace1767f4dbf656d494475323c839b42f25a3876a" "q-134173/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-134173/selection/ab3343a580c9ecbbb4e27d0c43b67b7d3815a6806a811b62927c9243c7c87034" "q-134173/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-134173" :question/id #uuid "f14a5fa1-39fe-5e33-b04b-72da56d8f87d" :question/math-academy-id "q-134173" :question/problem "| **Time Spent Practicing, \nin hours ($x$)** | $4$ | $5$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Points Scored ($y$)** | $4$ | $8$ | $12$ | $16$ |\n\nThe table above shows Mary's time practicing her jump shot each week and the number of points she scores in the Friday varsity basketball game. Compute the covariance of the data sets given that the means are $\\overset{―}{x}=6$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=10.$" :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(4-6)(4-10)+(5-6)(8-10)+(7-6)(12-10)+(8-6)(16-10)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-2)(-6)+(-1)(-2)+(1)(2)+(2)(6)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[12+2+2+12] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 28 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-134173/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cee807c1-dd86-5b0e-a595-5c5754c47e4c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-134173"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-134211/selection/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" :answer/id #uuid "9e9d942f-91c2-5475-8351-b