 --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Grades, in percents ($y$)** | $64$ | $78$ | $76$ | $82$ |\n\nThe table above shows the relationship between the amount of time four of Mike's classmates watch TV per week and their overall math scores. Compute the covariance of the data sets given that the means are $\\overset{―}{x}=10$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=75.$" :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(4\\,-\\,10)(64\\,-\\,75)+(8\\,-\\,10)(78\\,-\\,75)+(12\\,-\\,10)(76\\,-\\,75)+(16\\,-\\,10)(82\\,-\\,75)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-6)(-11)+(-2)(3)+(2)(1)+(6)(7)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[66-6+2+42] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 104 \\\\  & =26.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-134211/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cee807c1-dd86-5b0e-a595-5c5754c47e4c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-134211"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
